# Every text file is LF in every checkout, Windows included. The npm package
# ships LF, the installers and hooks compare bytes, and Bash cannot run a
# script with CR in it, so a CRLF checkout would test a tree no user gets.
# CRLF handling is tested with fixtures that carry CRLF on purpose.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The release ZIP is `git archive HEAD`. The READMEs show these files from raw
# GitHub URLs and the Pages site deploys from the checkout, so the ZIP does not
# need them; leaving them out keeps it about 2 MB instead of 20.
site/intro.mp4 export-ignore
docs/assets/*.gif export-ignore
docs/assets/*.png export-ignore
docs/assets/*.jpg export-ignore
